#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:51
msgid ""
"The CMUcam4 captures an image of the line at 30 frames per second and feeds "
"the color tracking image to the Arduino Mega via one of the three Serial "
"lines. The Arduino Mega then processes this image (please see Software "
"Description below) and delivers motor speed and turn commands to the PID "
"controller via another Serial line. The PID controller in turn provides the "
"Arduino Mega with encoder counts for both right and left wheels, which "
"allows us to keep track of our position and heading relative to gate 0."
msgstr ""
"CMUcam4 menangkap gambar garis pada 30 frame per detik dan mengumpankan "
"gambar pelacakan warna ke Arduino Mega melalui salah satu dari tiga jalur "
"Serial. Arduino Mega kemudian memproses gambar ini (silakan lihat Deskripsi "
"Perangkat Lunak di bawah) dan mengirimkan perintah kecepatan motor dan "
"belokan ke pengendali PID melalui jalur Serial lainnya. Pengendali PID pada "
"gilirannya memberikan Arduino Mega hitungan encoder untuk roda kanan dan "
"kiri, yang memungkinkan kami melacak posisi dan arah hadap kami relatif "
"terhadap gerbang 0."

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:59
msgid ""
"The PID controller (MD-25) is made by Robot-Electronics in the UK. It drives"
" two geared DC brush motors with motor shaft magnetic encoders. The LCD "
"screen is for debugging purposes. We had two power rails, 12V for motors and"
" 5V for logic, sharing the same ground and both sourced from a single 12V "
"rechargeable battery."
msgstr ""
"Pengendali PID (MD-25) dibuat oleh Robot-Electronics di Inggris. Ia "
"menggerakkan dua motor sikat DC bergigi dengan encoder magnetik poros motor."
" Layar LCD digunakan untuk keperluan debug. Kami memiliki dua rel daya, 12V "
"untuk motor dan 5V untuk logika, berbagi ground yang sama dan keduanya "
"bersumber dari satu baterai isi ulang 12V."

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:64
msgid ""
"We initially planned to make a prototype from a wood base to get us into the"
" programming phase quickly, then work on a faster, more reliable base such "
"as an RC car. However, we found that the prototype was very reliable and "
"easy to work with, so we kept it for the final design. Waterproofing for the"
" body consisted of a layer of cellophane wrap under a layer of packaging "
"tape. Rain however leaked through the packaging tape but fortunately not "
"through the cellophane wrap. The camera was covered by a square of plastic "
"from a Ziploc bag since we found that the \"filter\" improved the camera's "
"ability to ignore small patches of the line that, to the camera, looked like"
" the background concrete."
msgstr ""
"Kami awalnya berencana membuat prototipe dari basis kayu untuk membawa kami "
"ke fase pemrograman dengan cepat, kemudian mengerjakan basis yang lebih "
"cepat dan lebih andal seperti mobil RC. Namun, kami menemukan bahwa "
"prototipe sangat andal dan mudah untuk dikerjakan, jadi kami "
"mempertahankannya untuk desain akhir. Kedap air untuk bodi terdiri dari "
"lapisan pembungkus selofan di bawah lapisan selotip pengemasan. Namun hujan "
"bocor melalui selotip pengemasan tetapi untungnya tidak melalui pembungkus "
"selofan. Kamera ditutupi oleh sepotong plastik persegi dari kantong Ziploc "
"karena kami menemukan bahwa \"filter\" tersebut meningkatkan kemampuan "
"kamera untuk mengabaikan bercak-bercak kecil garis yang, bagi kamera, "
"terlihat seperti beton latar belakang."

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:75
msgid "Algorithm Description"
msgstr "Deskripsi Algoritma"

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:78
msgid "Background"
msgstr "Latar Belakang"

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:80
msgid ""
"We use the CMUcam4 in color tracking mode with YUV mode enabled, which gives"
" us a binary image representation of the line. The camera software filters "
"out anything that is not white (i.e. the background) and puts an \"on\" "
"pixel where there is a line (where it is white). We use YUV mode so that "
"color tracking is insensitive to the intensity of light, so that our robot "
"can function under a wide variety of conditions including indoors and "
"outdoors."
msgstr ""
"Kami menggunakan CMUcam4 dalam mode pelacakan warna dengan mode YUV "
"diaktifkan, yang memberi kami representasi gambar biner dari garis. "
"Perangkat lunak kamera menyaring apa pun yang bukan putih (mis. latar "
"belakang) dan menempatkan piksel \"on\" di mana ada garis (di mana itu "
"putih). Kami menggunakan mode YUV sehingga pelacakan warna tidak peka "
"terhadap intensitas cahaya, sehingga robot kami dapat berfungsi dalam "
"berbagai kondisi termasuk dalam dan luar ruangan."

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:88
msgid "Line Following"
msgstr "Pengikutan Garis"

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:90
msgid ""
"The CMUcam4 provides our Arduino chip with an 80 by 60 binary image. We "
"sample 10 equally spaced rows of pixels from the image and calculate the "
"centroid of \"on\" pixels (see here: "
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centroid#Of_a_finite_set_of_points). We then "
"assume that the line lies on the centroid. By doing this on 10 different "
"rows in the image, we get a good approximation of the line by connecting the"
" dots. We can then use this data by finding how far each point on the line "
"is from the vertical line that lies at the center of the image to get a "
"value representing how curved the line is. This can be seen as something "
"like finding the area between the tangent line and a curve and using that "
"area to determine how much we need to turn. The sign determines if the turn "
"is left or right, while the magnitude determines how much we need to turn to"
" follow the line. As you would expect, if we measured zero area, then the "
"line is directly in front of the robot and is a straight line. If the "
"magnitude of the area is large, then the robot needs to turn to maintain "
"attempt to minimize the magnitude of this area."
msgstr ""
"CMUcam4 memberikan chip Arduino kami gambar biner 80 kali 60. Kami mengambil"
" sampel 10 baris piksel berjarak sama dari gambar dan menghitung centroid "
"dari piksel \"on\" (lihat di sini: "
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centroid#Of_a_finite_set_of_points). Kami "
"kemudian mengasumsikan bahwa garis terletak pada centroid. Dengan melakukan "
"ini pada 10 baris berbeda dalam gambar, kami mendapatkan aproksimasi yang "
"baik dari garis dengan menghubungkan titik-titik. Kami kemudian dapat "
"menggunakan data ini dengan mencari seberapa jauh setiap titik pada garis "
"dari garis vertikal yang terletak di pusat gambar untuk mendapatkan nilai "
"yang mewakili seberapa melengkung garis tersebut. Ini dapat dilihat seperti "
"mencari luas antara garis singgung dan sebuah kurva dan menggunakan luas itu"
" untuk menentukan seberapa banyak kami perlu berbelok. Tanda menentukan "
"apakah belokan ke kiri atau kanan, sementara besarnya menentukan seberapa "
"banyak kami perlu berbelok untuk mengikuti garis. Seperti yang Anda duga, "
"jika kami mengukur luas nol, maka garis tepat berada di depan robot dan "
"merupakan garis lurus. Jika besarnya luas besar, maka robot perlu berbelok "
"untuk mempertahankan upaya meminimalkan besarnya luas ini."

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:107
msgid "Decision Points"
msgstr "Titik Keputusan"

#: ../../legacy/cmucam4/mobot.rst:109
msgid ""
"To determine if the robot is at a decision point, we take the data the "
"camera gathers from line following and check to see how many average center "
"points appear in black space. This works based on the assumption that the "
"average point between two lines should not be on either line, unless the "
"lines are the same line. If the robot detects multiple average points in the"
" black space, it can conclude that there must be two lines here. Then it "
"selects the appropriate turn and biases its turning toward that direction "
"until it sees only one line."
msgstr ""
"Untuk menentukan apakah robot berada di titik keputusan, kami mengambil data"
" yang dikumpulkan kamera dari pengikutan garis dan memeriksa berapa banyak "
"titik pusat rata-rata yang muncul di ruang hitam. Ini bekerja berdasarkan "
"asumsi bahwa titik rata-rata antara dua garis seharusnya tidak berada di "
"salah satu garis, kecuali jika garis-garis tersebut adalah garis yang sama. "
"Jika robot mendeteksi beberapa titik rata-rata di ruang hitam, ia dapat "
"menyimpulkan bahwa pasti ada dua garis di sini. Kemudian ia memilih belokan "
"yang sesuai dan membiaskan belokannya ke arah itu sampai ia hanya melihat "
"satu garis."

